<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Buenaventura upped.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Buenaventura upped.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Robert Fleming analyst Warwick Jones said he had raised his rating for Peru's Compania de Minas Buenaventura SA to buy from long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- In a Feb 22 analysis, Jones wrote that the mining company had been helped by a Peruvian court decision that raised its and Newmont Mining Corp's stakes in the Yanacocha gold mine, the biggest in Latin America.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Buenaventura can complete the acquisition of 11.3 percent, lifting its equity to 42.6 percent, at a cost of nearly $50 million,&quot; he wrote.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Although this is about 20 percent more than Buenaventura originally hoped to pay, we think it got a bargain.  We think the value of the equity could be as high as $200 million.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's American Depositary Receipts closed at 17-7/8 on Friday in New York.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
